 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A third cyclone in weeks is heading for India's east coast. Who's in its path?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Cyclone Akvan formed over the Bay of Bengal on Monday, India's weather department says. That night, Sri Lanka's forecasters placed it about six hundred forty kilometers from Trincomalee, and warned fishers and naval crews to stay away."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "India's weather department expects Akvan to become a very severe cyclonic storm, with winds up to one hundred forty-five kilometers an hour. It says the storm is likely to cross the Andhra Pradesh coast between Nellore and Tuni on Friday. Local reports say the track has shifted."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "In Odisha, officials aim to move about two hundred four thousand people, local media report. Ganjam district had evacuated twenty-seven hundred by Tuesday evening. Akvan follows Cyclone Arnab on October twenty-eighth and Cyclone Murasu on November third."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Akvan reach land as a very severe cyclone? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
