 "upload": {
  "title": "Cyclone Akvan Takes Aim at India's Andhra Coast #shorts",
  "description": "Cyclone Akvan formed over the Bay of Bengal on November 16. India's weather department expects it to become a very severe cyclonic storm and cross the Andhra Pradesh coast between Nellore and Tuni around November 20 — the third cyclone on that coast in weeks, after Arnab and Murasu. Odisha aims to evacuate about 204,000 people.\n\nSources: India Meteorological Department, Sri Lanka Department of Meteorology (via Newswire, Ada Derana), Business Standard, india.com, Odisha TV, Ommcom News, Al Jazeera (based on search-result excerpts). The storm track on the map is illustrative and positions are approximate.\n\n#climate #weather #cyclone #india",
